Yes. This class is actually a good candidate for extracting the retry configuration into a separate class, especially because you already have the same Reactor retry pattern in P2P Edge.

I would avoid putting more retry-specific logging into TrackingResourceWebClientHelper. Instead, make the retry configuration reusable.

1. Create a separate RetryConfig

For example:

config/
    RetryConfig.java

package com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.config;

import com.cardinalhealth.ofl.next.logging.library.LogBuilder;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.web.reactive.function.client.WebClientResponseException;
import reactor.util.retry.Retry;
import reactor.util.retry.Retry.RetrySignal;

import java.time.Duration;

import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.BACKOFF_MAX_ATTEMPTS;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.BACKOFF_MIN_DURATION;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.BOUNDARY_HTTP_ERROR;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.COMPONENT;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.ERROR_TYPE;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.EXCEPTION_CLASS;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.JITTER;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.MAXBACKOFF_DURATION;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.MESSAGE;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.STACK_TRACE;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.STATUS_CODE;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.TRACKING_RESOURCE_WEBCLIENT_HELPER;
import static com.cardinalhealth.advship.tracking.api.service.webclient.TrackingResourceConstants.UNHANDLED_EXCEPTION;

@Slf4j
@Configuration
public class RetryConfig {

    public Retry createExponentialRetry() {
        return Retry.backoff(
                    BACKOFF_MAX_ATTEMPTS,
                    Duration.ofSeconds(BACKOFF_MIN_DURATION)
                )
                .maxBackoff(Duration.ofSeconds(MAXBACKOFF_DURATION))
                .jitter(JITTER)
                .filter(this::isRetryable)
                .doBeforeRetry(this::logRetry)
                .onRetryExhaustedThrow((spec, signal) -> {
                    logRetryExhausted(signal);

                    return new RuntimeException(
                        "Retries exhausted for the tracking-resource request",
                        signal.failure()
                    );
                });
    }

    private boolean isRetryable(Throwable throwable) {

        if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
            int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();

            return statusCode >= INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR
                    && statusCode < BOUNDARY_HTTP_ERROR;
        }

        return true;
    }

    private void logRetry(RetrySignal signal) {

        Throwable throwable = signal.failure();

        LogBuilder logBuilder = new LogBuilder()
                .withMessage("Retrying tracking-resource API request")
                .withField(
                    "retryAttempt",
                    signal.totalRetries() + 1
                )
                .withField(
                    ERROR_TYPE,
                    throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException
                        ? "WEBCLIENT_EXCEPTION"
                        : UNHANDLED_EXCEPTION
                )
                .withField(
                    EXCEPTION_CLASS,
                    throwable.getClass().getName()
                )
                .withField(
                    MESSAGE,
                    throwable.getMessage()
                )
                .withField(
                    COMPONENT,
                    TRACKING_RESOURCE_WEBCLIENT_HELPER
                );

        if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
            logBuilder.withField(
                STATUS_CODE,
                ex.getStatusCode().value()
            );
        }

        log.error(
            logBuilder.toString(),
            throwable
        );
    }

    private void logRetryExhausted(RetrySignal signal) {

        Throwable throwable = signal.failure();

        log.error(
            new LogBuilder()
                .withMessage(
                    "Retries exhausted for tracking-resource API request"
                )
                .withField(
                    "totalRetries",
                    signal.totalRetries()
                )
                .withField(
                    EXCEPTION_CLASS,
                    throwable.getClass().getName()
                )
                .withField(
                    MESSAGE,
                    throwable.getMessage()
                )
                .withField(
                    COMPONENT,
                    TRACKING_RESOURCE_WEBCLIENT_HELPER
                )
                .toString(),
            throwable
        );
    }
}

2. Inject it into TrackingResourceWebClientHelper

Add:

private final RetryConfig retryConfig;

and update the constructor:

public TrackingResourceWebClientHelper(
        ObjectMapper objectMapper,
        RetryConfig retryConfig) {

    this.objectMapper = objectMapper;
    this.retryConfig = retryConfig;
}

Then change:

.retryWhen(createExponentialRetry(new LogBuilder()))

to:

.retryWhen(retryConfig.createExponentialRetry())


---

3. Remove the retry code from the helper

You can completely remove this method:

private Retry createExponentialRetry(LogBuilder logBuilder) {
    ...
}

And you can also remove the retry-related isRetryable() from this class because it now belongs in RetryConfig.

This makes the helper responsible for the API call, while RetryConfig is responsible for retry behavior:

TrackingResourceWebClientHelper
        |
        | retryWhen()
        ↓
    RetryConfig
        |
        ├── isRetryable()
        ├── doBeforeRetry()
        └── retry exhausted logging

4. One important improvement over the current implementation

Your current isRetryable() logs every exception before deciding whether it is retryable:

log.error(...);
if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ...)

That means even a 400 or 404 gets logged there.

With the new approach:

Exception
   ↓
isRetryable()
   ↓
400 → false → no retry logging
500 → true
   ↓
doBeforeRetry()
   ↓
log retry attempt

So the retry log specifically represents an actual retry, which is cleaner.

5. Your existing handleErrorMap() should stay

I would not remove the logging from handleErrorMap() yet.

That logging has a different purpose:

RetryConfig
    → logs retry attempts

handleErrorMap()
    → logs final API error / maps exception

You may eventually find that some of the final-error logging is duplicated because onRetryExhaustedThrow() also logs. After testing the complete flow, we can decide whether the exhaustion log should remain in both places.

Expected result

For a 503:

API → 503
 ↓
isRetryable → true
 ↓
Retry attempt 1 → LOG
 ↓
API → 503
 ↓
Retry attempt 2 → LOG
 ↓
API → 503
 ↓
Retry attempt 3 → LOG
 ↓
Retries exhausted → LOG final exception
 ↓
handleErrorMap()

For a 400:

API → 400
 ↓
isRetryable → false
 ↓
No retry
 ↓
handleErrorMap()

This is the approach I'd recommend for this class because it gives you the same Reactor-based pattern as P2P Edge, while keeping the retry configuration out of the WebClient helper.